{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347241-what-would-you-like-to-see-in-the-st-guide-crucible-of-legends","id":1347241,"title":"What would you like to see in the ST Guide? (Crucible of Legends)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-11-09T08:07:01-08:00","id":1347241,"title":"What would you like to see in the ST Guide? (Crucible of Legends)","content":"There is already some info floating around about what will be in the Storyteller's Guide (Crucible of Legends). For instance we know it will have QCs for every Exalt type including those whose books will come after the ST Guide.<br /> <br /> What else would you like to see in the guide?<br /> <br /> <br /> Personally I'd like to get more information on which Lore elements are being kept intentionally vague in 3e. We know 3e leaves more things intentionally vague than 2e did so that ST's can have more leeway - but because so much of 3e is yet to be published, it's hard to guess when something is being left vague intentionally vs when the lore for it simply isn't out yet. Some of it has been clarified in the ask a dev threads, but it would be helpful to have that info available in official material since many STs will never see those threads.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T08:25:45-08:00","id":1347245,"title":"","content":"I'm hoping that in the rush of new and revisited Exalt types, they don't neglect that which hails from the Wyld, the dead, and the unclassifiable. 1e's Storyteller's Companion had a whole chapter on spirits, as a reminder - it wasn't <i>all</i> Exalts.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T09:18:55-08:00","id":1347258,"title":"","content":"I want easy and fast NPC rules I can use with guides on how to make balanced (simple things like what is the power level of Double 8 ?), cool (template for things like elemental or supernatural affinity you can easily apply to NPCs to give them a personnal quirk) and fun (generic ideas on how to turn a mechanic into a fun one through description or twists), so I can either replace my homebrew system I use for NPCs or integrate it in my homebrew system.<br /> <br /> I haven't read all the Realm yet, but I got the feeling I have enough lore and world building stuff with Core, Dragon blooded, The Realm and Lunars : FatG to keep different campaigns running for very long. I don't oppose having more stuff of course, but I think I have quite enough materials. What I lack is &quot;mechanical content&quot; that allows me to quickly and easily incarnate the cool ideas that already exist in a challenging way.<br /> <br /> I'm always interested in more cosmological stuff because that's my &quot;literature preference&quot;, but I also know that explaining mysterious cosmological stuff can sometimes make it dull, so I'd be fine with not having things along this way.<br /> <br /> One thing I would love, though, is advice on how to handle Yu-Shan, because I have absolutely no idea whatsoever on how to handle adventures, interactions, bureaucracy, politics, and intrigues through gods and Yu-Shan, and I'm very sad for it because I love the idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T09:23:49-08:00","id":1347259,"title":"","content":"Eclipse Charms<br /> Antagonists NPCs<br /> Maybe some rules about Creating/Ruling an Empire<br /> I've always wanted some rules about chase (based on the Initiative system)<br /> And because I'm not so good at creating adventures maybe a chapter on Sanbox adventure or Ideas for some adventure in every Direction<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12575-gaara","name":"Gaara","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T09:25:08-08:00","id":1347260,"title":"","content":"A bureaucracy system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T09:44:44-08:00","id":1347263,"title":"","content":"More examples of sorcerous workings, and advice on adjudicating the system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T11:35:09-08:00","id":1347298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347241-what-would-you-like-to-see-in-the-st-guide-crucible-of-legends?p=1347260#post1347260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A bureaucracy system.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or even just examples of how it is used honestly. I don't think it need be (Or even shoudl be) CRM. But like...examples of what you acutally <i>do</i> with the Ability wouldn't hurt. SImilar with Occult, Survival, and a few other Abilities to be honest.<br /> <br /> Mind, this has been apparently something mentioned as to will be the case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T11:42:29-08:00","id":1347299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347241-what-would-you-like-to-see-in-the-st-guide-crucible-of-legends?p=1347298#post1347298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or even just examples of how it is used honestly. I don't think it need be (Or even shoudl be) CRM. But like...examples of what you acutally <i>do</i> with the Ability wouldn't hurt. SImilar with Occult, Survival, and a few other Abilities to be honest.<br /> <br /> Mind, this has been apparently something mentioned as to will be the case.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's true that I don't really know what to do with Occult, except having Occult Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T12:11:53-08:00","id":1347305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347241-what-would-you-like-to-see-in-the-st-guide-crucible-of-legends?p=1347299#post1347299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's true that I don't really know what to do with Occult, except having Occult Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually find Occult to be one that I can make sense of, but to be fair I've played for a while.Thinking of rituals and magic shenanigans falls under Occult, as do Workings (obviously) but also most knowledge about various magical entities can often be rolled with Occult as well as Lore, depending on exactly what you want to know.<br /> <br /> I second the bureaucracy thing. There needs to be more for it. If there's space I'd like a system that makes the Athletics speed charms related to footraces do something?<br /> There are a bunch of other things like how to structure cool social scenes and how to handle investigations. Honestly, I need to find my old post because I feel like there was more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8097-wern212","name":"wern212","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8097_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T12:16:28-08:00","id":1347308,"title":"","content":"First and foremost, advice about creating challenges that affect most of the party (ie combat, or a big party or something) when you have characters with such radically varying capacities. That's probably the part of DMing Exalted that worries me the most.<br /> <br /> On a similar note, a &quot;how to use social influence&quot; section would also be helpful. Advice about using it against the players without frustrating them, on how much offense VS defense to give npcs, on balancing &quot;let this be useful&quot; against &quot;they can just talk their way through everything with no danger,&quot; stuff like that.<br /> <br /> Finally, on a mechanical note... Charms for QCs. While the simplified version of the stats is useful, the core book gives no help with the part that's actually HARD-- inventing Charms. I'd like to see... oh... Let's say 5 decisive attack charms, 5 dodge/parry charms, 5 soak/hardness charms, and 10 social charms. Each one a simple and generic mechanic, with a few suggestions on how to fluff it and maybe a variant or two. Powers that put a new spin on the fight but could represent a wide variety of actions, so I can easily put together a hostile forge god that FEELS like a god of steel and fire without having to write 5 charms <br /> <br /> (Ie, something like &quot;Damage Aura: deals (1/2 Essence) initiative damage to everything in close range, or lethal damage on targets in Crash. This could represent raging flames, a shroud of ghosts, a long thrashing tail, or something similar. Variant: For something more like a layer of spines, increase the damage to (Essence), but only affects targets who hit you with a melee attack.&quot;)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T12:36:56-08:00","id":1347314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grod_the_giant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347241-what-would-you-like-to-see-in-the-st-guide-crucible-of-legends?p=1347308#post1347308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Finally, on a mechanical note... Charms for QCs.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like Exigents is the book that's going to be this, not Crucible. I wouldn't be opposed to it, but I think that would be a better fit anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8097-wern212","name":"wern212","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8097_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T12:48:08-08:00","id":1347316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grod_the_giant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347241-what-would-you-like-to-see-in-the-st-guide-crucible-of-legends?p=1347308#post1347308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First and foremost, advice about creating challenges that affect most of the party (ie combat, or a big party or something) when you have characters with such radically varying capacities. That's probably the part of DMing Exalted that worries me the most.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good idea. I found that, in combat, having a mix of enemies (more and less powerful) for different PCs to deal with, and outside of combat the key is to have plenty of different situations so everyone can shine. But I think a lot more can be said.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Finally, on a mechanical note... Charms for QCs. While the simplified version of the stats is useful, the core book gives no help with the part that's actually HARD-- inventing Charms. I'd like to see... oh... Let's say 5 decisive attack charms, 5 dodge/parry charms, 5 soak/hardness charms, and 10 social charms. Each one a simple and generic mechanic, with a few suggestions on how to fluff it and maybe a variant or two. Powers that put a new spin on the fight but could represent a wide variety of actions, so I can easily put together a hostile forge god that FEELS like a god of steel and fire without having to write 5 charms </div> </div> </div>That's a great idea. Though Exigents would probably help a lot with it. I'm not really sure how it'll work in practice though, I think charm guidelines are quite tricky.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T14:19:26-08:00","id":1347322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wern212</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347241-what-would-you-like-to-see-in-the-st-guide-crucible-of-legends?p=1347314#post1347314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like Exigents is the book that's going to be this, not Crucible. I wouldn't be opposed to it, but I think that would be a better fit anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably, yeah. What I'm thinking of is to Extigent Charm creation rules what QCs are to player characters-- general archetypes cut down to bare essentials, rather than full-on Charm trees. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347241-what-would-you-like-to-see-in-the-st-guide-crucible-of-legends?p=1347316#post1347316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not really sure how it'll work in practice though, I think charm guidelines are quite tricky.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh gods, agreed. I've done a fair chunk of game design, and I wouldn't want to write <i>anything </i>like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T23:47:16-08:00","id":1347414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grod_the_giant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347241-what-would-you-like-to-see-in-the-st-guide-crucible-of-legends?p=1347322#post1347322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably, yeah. What I'm thinking of is to Extigent Charm creation rules what QCs are to player characters-- general archetypes cut down to bare essentials, rather than full-on Charm trees.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now, with the <b>massive</b> caveat that this information comes from the previous Ex3 dev team, I believe there was the idea of a massive list of bare-bones charm effects that you could slot a dice pool into and give it to your QC with some fun flavor. Again, this dev team hasn't said they will continue that idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8097-wern212","name":"wern212","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8097_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-10T00:04:28-08:00","id":1347416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347241-what-would-you-like-to-see-in-the-st-guide-crucible-of-legends?p=1347259#post1347259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eclipse Charms<br /> And because I'm not so good at creating adventures maybe a chapter on Sanbox adventure or Ideas for some adventure in every Direction</div> </div> </div> </div>Seconding this! I'd like to have a practical chapter about what kind of stories suit different exalt types and advice, how to turn those large ideas into gameable challenges. Something like the Exalted Campaign Types in 2e, but a bit more detailed. For example, advice how to structure your encounters so they offer something interesting to overcompetent Solars or what kind of missions a Sworn Kinship in the middle of House intrigue might take. Something to ease a new Storyteller's entry into Exalted.<br /> (I am also very interested in the dev intention in them, I want to see what kind of campaigns and adventures they expect the system is suited for.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24320-taleksi","name":"Taleksi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24320_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-11T20:23:29-08:00","id":1347827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347241-what-would-you-like-to-see-in-the-st-guide-crucible-of-legends?p=1347259#post1347259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe some rules about Creating/Ruling an Empire</div> </div> </div> </div>Including states, churches, nations and businesses. Examples of organization sheets (Guild, Immaculate Order, Scarlet Empire, etc.)<br /> Bureaucratic system.<br /> Mass social system.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2150-rochedo","name":"Rochedo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2150_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-11T23:40:26-08:00","id":1347839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rochedo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347241-what-would-you-like-to-see-in-the-st-guide-crucible-of-legends?p=1347827#post1347827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Including states, churches, nations and businesses.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think nationalism has <i>quite </i>been invented yet in the setting.<br /> <br /> Moving on, I'd be fine with a more robust &quot;Bureaucracy system&quot; if these things didn't tend to reduce people to interchangeable cogs in said organizations' machines, kept running smooth regardless of context by the Solars' Bureaucracy Charms. Since that seems to keep happening <i>each time </i>these kinds of rules get introduced (see the Appendices in <i>Storyteller's Guide</i> and <i>Masters of Jade</i> in 2e), I'm happy with the Leadership rules we've got in 3e (the ST decides on the possibility of and how long a project might take, as well as complications that can threaten its success, the player can say how to deal with said complications, and then the success or failure of the project might create further complications).<br /> <br /> Especially given the way that the leadership rules in 2e present a situation that kinda resembles the Hacker Problem in modern RPGs; the one player with Bureaucracy ends up directing the empire's policies, while the other players sit and twiddle their thumbs, waiting for when they can go back to doing stuff. Except where the Decker's player in a game of Shadowrun might take half an hour of the table's time to resolve his hacking, but only have it take eighteen seconds of in-game time, the Eclipse commands the table's time to resolve stuff that takes <i>months</i> of in-game time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 11-12-2019, 07:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T04:09:25-08:00","id":1347854,"title":"","content":"Agreed, and I actually would love it if the ST Guide didn't just offer a replacement for that. But the bureaucracy system just needs to offer the players (or the ST) a bit more guidance.<br /> And the mercantile system is rather lacking, for that I would prefer more support.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8097-wern212","name":"wern212","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8097_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T04:21:22-08:00","id":1347857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wern212</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347241-what-would-you-like-to-see-in-the-st-guide-crucible-of-legends?p=1347854#post1347854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the bureaucracy system just needs to offer the players (or the ST) a bit more guidance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that the Leadership &quot;system&quot; in the core book is just &quot;wing it,&quot; I'm inclined to agree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T04:33:05-08:00","id":1347859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wern212</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347241-what-would-you-like-to-see-in-the-st-guide-crucible-of-legends?p=1347854#post1347854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the mercantile system is rather lacking, for that I would prefer more support.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, I love the Charms for it Solar, but I'm totally unskilled enough IRL to know how to use them in a fun way during games for trade, market and stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T07:47:59-08:00","id":1347895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grod_the_giant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347241-what-would-you-like-to-see-in-the-st-guide-crucible-of-legends?p=1347857#post1347857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given that the Leadership &amp;quot;system&amp;quot; in the core book is just &amp;quot;wing it,&amp;quot; I'm inclined to agree.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, just make some shit up is not rules and doesn't engage with the rest of the game or even the relevant charmsets or abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T09:23:52-08:00","id":1347923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grod_the_giant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347241-what-would-you-like-to-see-in-the-st-guide-crucible-of-legends?p=1347857#post1347857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given that the Leadership &quot;system&quot; in the core book is just &quot;wing it,&quot; I'm inclined to agree.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually disagree. I think the Leadership system is actually an interesting way to make that work, and I like the emphasis that if there's no reason to have projects fail they should just succeed.<br /> That being said because Bureaucracy has no tie-in to the system, there's basically nothing to do with Bureaucracy 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8097-wern212","name":"wern212","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8097_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T11:13:22-08:00","id":1347967,"title":"","content":"Honestly I mainly want a really solid chapter on running chronicles. Like I get by just fine, I've been running games for 20 years but it seemed like such a glaring oversight from the core book and I really wondered how the hell new players would manage. I'd like to see the standard stuff: different kinds of Exalted campaigns one could run, what elements make up a good campaign, pointers on things like story hooks and bringing characters together in Exalted, running Exaltations in game if you want to do that, what makes for compelling NPCs, some examples of cinema tropes that lend themselves well to Exalted, and so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229925-hello-i-did-up-a-scavenger-lands-map-based-on-3e\" target=\"_blank\">3e Scavenger Lands map</a><br /> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/a/NQewCv0\" target=\"_blank\">3e Combat tracker card</a><br /> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/uGrZk2r\" target=\"_blank\">2e Nexus map</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1079-megapope","name":"Megapope","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T13:21:42-08:00","id":1347996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347241-what-would-you-like-to-see-in-the-st-guide-crucible-of-legends?p=1347839#post1347839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think nationalism has <i>quite </i>been invented yet in the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>The existence of nations suggests otherwise.<br /> <br /> If nationalism didn't exist, people would be merely tribal (which is just <i>ethnic</i> nationalism) or associate only with people who held the same ideologies (which is virtually impossible without an internet that enables you to communicate with people across the world more often than people within your own local community).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T04:36:02-08:00","id":1348217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347241-what-would-you-like-to-see-in-the-st-guide-crucible-of-legends?p=1347996#post1347996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The existence of nations suggests otherwise.<br /> <br /> If nationalism didn't exist, people would be merely tribal (which is just <i>ethnic</i> nationalism) or associate only with people who held the same ideologies (which is virtually impossible without an internet that enables you to communicate with people across the world more often than people within your own local community).</div> </div> </div> </div>There were kingdoms and empires and city-states and such throughout human history, sure, but &quot;nationalism&quot; is a 19th/20th century construct-- particularly the idea of the state as a single ethnic/cultural unit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T04:52:17-08:00","id":1348227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grod_the_giant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347241-what-would-you-like-to-see-in-the-st-guide-crucible-of-legends?p=1348217#post1348217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There were kingdoms and empires and city-states and such throughout human history, sure, but &quot;nationalism&quot; is a 19th/20th century construct-- particularly the idea of the state as a single ethnic/cultural unit.</div> </div> </div> </div>We're talking about this:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rochedo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347241-what-would-you-like-to-see-in-the-st-guide-crucible-of-legends?p=1347827#post1347827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Including states, churches, nations and businesses. Examples of organization sheets (Guild, Immaculate Order, Scarlet Empire, etc.)<br /> Bureaucratic system.<br /> Mass social system.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not whether the Ancient Greek City States thought of themselves as culturally homogeneous (which is a weird derail, but I assure you that an Athenian identity existed long before the 1800s), or whether ethnonations are nations, or if Reynolds' deconstruction of medieval fuedal states as nations is valid.<br /> <br /> We're talking about a system for representing running a nation in play. I'd love to see one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 11-14-2019, 06:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T05:09:08-08:00","id":1348231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wern212</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347241-what-would-you-like-to-see-in-the-st-guide-crucible-of-legends?p=1347923#post1347923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually disagree. I think the Leadership system is actually an interesting way to make that work, and I like the emphasis that if there's no reason to have projects fail they should just succeed.<br /> That being said because Bureaucracy has no tie-in to the system, there's basically nothing to do with Bureaucracy 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kinda. Ex3 treats Bureaucracy like a niche social ability rather than routing all influence rolls through Presence like 2e did, hence why Social Influence features the bargain action.<br /> The problem with doing that is that the Resources system doesn't allow much verisimilitude for haggling with monetary values, what's 20% off a Resources 5 purchase? How does that translate into Jade/Silver?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T05:42:09-08:00","id":1348240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347241-what-would-you-like-to-see-in-the-st-guide-crucible-of-legends?p=1348231#post1348231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kinda. Ex3 treats Bureaucracy like a niche social ability rather than routing all influence rolls through Presence like 2e did, hence why Social Influence features the bargain action.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe the Dev's have said that you can't roll for social actions with Bureaucracy, even bargain? But I could be mistaken there.<br /> But yeah, Bureaucracy doesn't have a ton to do and Resources are rather abstract. I hope ST Guide helps with this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8097-wern212","name":"wern212","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8097_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T05:53:24-08:00","id":1348243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347241-what-would-you-like-to-see-in-the-st-guide-crucible-of-legends?p=1347996#post1347996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If nationalism didn't exist,</div> </div> </div> </div>This is how medieval society worked.<br /> <br /> And I wish was how my country worked today, but sadly it is not. I mean, I can understand why many Irish, Welsh and Scottish people feel they must resort to Nationalism, but I can't agree with it in the long run. (English Nationalists have no excuse.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> or associate only with people who held the same ideologies (which is virtually impossible without an internet that enables you to communicate with people across the world more often than people within your own local community). </div> </div> </div>If there's only one ideology in power that 99% of the populace go with, it's fine. (Sucked for the Jews though.)<br /> Or people are just non-ideological and accept that they must bow to their government or be killed, and whether that government is legitimate is something best not thought too much about.<br /> <br /> <br /> But basically I think is an argument about semantics because you're talking about different things.<br /> <br /> I think Grod and Alucard are talking about the academic poli-sci definition of Nationalism and Nation-States (which is a distinct ideology), while I think John and Sunder are talking about the non-academic definition where Nation is synonymous with Country or State. Like when you say the Nation of the USA or the Nation of the United Kingdom (neither of which are Nations in the academic and ideological sense, but are clearly things people call Nations, hence the United Nations).<br /> <br /> <br /> Saying this, while nationalism might only exist in a proto-form in the Time of Tumult, I can actually see quite an interesting (if morally complex) game about building a (academic-definition) nation. And I can see some parts of that being part of a Bureaucracy system (such as building a... well, bureaucracy. Maybe creating firm borders. Maybe less so spreading a unified group-identity, promoting a particular view of history, etc. Those could be done via bureaucracy I guess... hmmm, I suppose in practice they are).<br /> <br /> (I mean... obviously some would argue that Nation-Building by its very idea is attacking the basis of Nationalism, but Exalted is quite happy to deconstruct ideologies!)<br /> <br /> In fact, one of the PCs in the essence 5 game is doing this. (And it's almost as bad as you'd expect. I mean, there hasn't been any actual genocide, but it's caused a lot of civil and external war, an inquisition, purges of priests and nobles, etc, etc.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway...<br /> Certainly I can see why people argue for a system about running a State. Though I can also see Alucard's worry about it, certainly previous editions had their issues. And I personally enjoy the personalisation of power within a monarchy, in terms of running games. (Ie, you bring your State together by going and socialising with regional nobles, assassinating your enemies, etc. Rather than rolling dice to represent administrative skill. Although of course if you don't what's the point of the ability and charms?)<br /> Perhaps something just for downtime.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 11-13-2019, 09:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T08:59:18-08:00","id":1348273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wern212</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347241-what-would-you-like-to-see-in-the-st-guide-crucible-of-legends?p=1348240#post1348240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe the Dev's have said that you can't roll for social actions with Bureaucracy, even bargain?</div> </div> </div> </div>If they have then they need to tighten up the Social Influence rules, because the book states &quot;(Charisma, Manipulation, or Appearance) plus a relevant Ability&quot; suggesting it's more the individual Storyteller's call.<br /> <br /> The bargain action is actually based on something Bureaucracy did in 1st edition before 2nd edition made it almost exclusively about organisation management <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>1e Exalted Core</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">BRIBES AND BUREAUCRACY Bribery and corruption are the way of the world. Often, characters will not just need to bribe officials to circumvent the law or have a special exception made, but will be forced to pay off officials to get them to do their jobs at all. Paying off an official who wishes to collect money to do her job requires no roll but may be a Resources \u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 expense, depending on what it is the character wants. Convincing an official to accept a bribe she isn't expecting requires a Manipulation + Bureaucracy roll. The difficulty of this roll depends on the probity of the official and how severe the punishment will he if she is caught accepting the bribe. Obviously, such bribes also have a Resources cost, and the bribing character must he able to pay it. Note that, in many cases, an official who chooses not to accept the bribe will still take the money and simply not honor the agreement.</div> </div> </div> </div>Finally, my group used it like that in the playtest and reported such.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T09:03:18-08:00","id":1348274,"title":"","content":"Also there's a non-zero number of Bureaucracy Charms that enhance social influence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wern212</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347241-what-would-you-like-to-see-in-the-st-guide-crucible-of-legends?p=1348240#post1348240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe the Dev's have said that you can't roll for social actions with Bureaucracy, even bargain?</div> </div> </div> </div>At this point, I have to ask, could you cite this please?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 11-13-2019, 01:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T10:06:04-08:00","id":1348283,"title":"","content":"removed to private message","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-14T00:51:33-08:00","id":1348434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347241-what-would-you-like-to-see-in-the-st-guide-crucible-of-legends?p=1348273#post1348273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they have then they need to tighten up the Social Influence rules, because the book states &quot;(Charisma, Manipulation, or Appearance) plus a relevant Ability&quot; suggesting it's more the individual Storyteller's call.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1137002#post1137002\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1137002#post1137002\"> Ask the Devs - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1137002#post1137002\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1137002#post1137002 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Dear Exalted fans, as you may be aware from the latest Onyx Path Monday Meeting notes (http://theonyxpath.com/princes-gambit-joy-exalted-plans-monday-meeting-notes/), Robert Vance and I have been honored with the opportunity to take on line editor duties for Exalted Third Edition. As part of that, we want to make ourselves available to the community as a resource to keep you informed as best we can about the line. Obviously there will be some questions we can't answer! But when we're not working on upcoming books, we'll drop in to touch base. We'll be using this thread as our port of call so that we </div> </div> </div><br /> So, this is the Vance comment I am basing this on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8097-wern212","name":"wern212","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8097_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-14T01:35:55-08:00","id":1348438,"title":"","content":"Yeah, looks solid.<br /> Either the previous developers were fine with situational use of Bureaucracy for social rolls or didn't catch our mistake.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-14T02:35:37-08:00","id":1348444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347241-what-would-you-like-to-see-in-the-st-guide-crucible-of-legends?p=1348243#post1348243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is how medieval society worked.<br /> <br /> And I wish was how my country worked today, but sadly it is not. I mean, I can understand why many Irish, Welsh and Scottish people feel they must resort to Nationalism, but I can't agree with it in the long run. (English Nationalists have no excuse.)<br /> <br /> <br /> If there's only one ideology in power that 99% of the populace go with, it's fine. (Sucked for the Jews though.)<br /> Or people are just non-ideological and accept that they must bow to their government or be killed, and whether that government is legitimate is something best not thought too much about.<br /> <br /> <br /> But basically I think is an argument about semantics because you're talking about different things.<br /> <br /> I think Grod and Alucard are talking about the academic poli-sci definition of Nationalism and Nation-States (which is a distinct ideology), while I think John and Sunder are talking about the non-academic definition where Nation is synonymous with Country or State. Like when you say the Nation of the USA or the Nation of the United Kingdom (neither of which are Nations in the academic and ideological sense, but are clearly things people call Nations, hence the United Nations).<br /> <br /> <br /> Saying this, while nationalism might only exist in a proto-form in the Time of Tumult, I can actually see quite an interesting (if morally complex) game about building a (academic-definition) nation. And I can see some parts of that being part of a Bureaucracy system (such as building a... well, bureaucracy. Maybe creating firm borders. Maybe less so spreading a unified group-identity, promoting a particular view of history, etc. Those could be done via bureaucracy I guess... hmmm, I suppose in practice they are).<br /> <br /> (I mean... obviously some would argue that Nation-Building by its very idea is attacking the basis of Nationalism, but Exalted is quite happy to deconstruct ideologies!)<br /> <br /> In fact, one of the PCs in the essence 5 game is doing this. (And it's almost as bad as you'd expect. I mean, there hasn't been any actual genocide, but it's caused a lot of civil and external war, an inquisition, purges of priests and nobles, etc, etc.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway...<br /> Certainly I can see why people argue for a system about running a State. Though I can also see Alucard's worry about it, certainly previous editions had their issues. And I personally enjoy the personalisation of power within a monarchy, in terms of running games. (Ie, you bring your State together by going and socialising with regional nobles, assassinating your enemies, etc. Rather than rolling dice to represent administrative skill. Although of course if you don't what's the point of the ability and charms?)<br /> Perhaps something just for downtime.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't disagree that people are using different definitions of words, just that the conversation started based on what was clearly <i>not</i> the pure &quot;academic&quot; use of the word, and that attempts at clarity in the discussion led to something of a derail (Wikipedia suggests the Byzantine Empire, Fifteenth Century England or the Dutch Republic as the first &quot;nations&quot;, if not the medieval feudal states, ethnonations or the city-states -- this doesn't seem incongruous with the Realm proper as a &quot;nation&quot;).<br /> <br /> Still, state-building (if that's more academically acceptable?) is a fertile ground for RPG stories, and I'd like to see it supported. If you could link me to an academic definition of &quot;nation&quot; (I freely admit that I don't know what a nation is in the academic sense), I'd love to educate myself (as introducing academic nations to Exalted seems like an epic social quest -- from my inference, it could be the basis of a fantastic campaign, so I'd love to see rules which facilitate this).<br /> <br /> But again, the point was a social system for managing a relatively large group of people organized under a single structure (be that a government, business, church or what-have-you).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 11-14-2019, 07:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-14T05:32:40-08:00","id":1348464,"title":"","content":"I think the leadership system might benefit from a random events table provided that the human element of it focused on things that could've been going on beneath the PCs notice. Also their inner circle are probably full fledged NPCs that the Storyteller wants to behave in a consistent manner.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-14T07:07:33-08:00","id":1348477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347241-what-would-you-like-to-see-in-the-st-guide-crucible-of-legends?p=1348444#post1348444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't disagree that people are using different definitions of words, just that the conversation started based on what was clearly <i>not</i> the pure &quot;academic&quot; use of the word, and that attempts at clarity in the discussion led to something of a derail</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, I was trying to move people beyond that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> this doesn't seem incongruous with the Realm proper as a &quot;nation&quot;). </div> </div> </div>Oddly for an Empire, it is somewhat reasonable to call the Realm a &quot;nation&quot;, due to the way their Satrapy system works.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Still, state-building (if that's more academically acceptable?) is a fertile ground for RPG stories, and I'd like to see it supported. </div> </div> </div>Whether or not there's a concrete system for it, or for some parts of it (and there's arguments for/against that, that have been brought up in this thread), it's definitely something an ST Guide for Exalted should address. It's not something that people who've mostly run, say, DnD, are going to have much experience with.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you could link me to an academic definition of &quot;nation&quot; </div> </div> </div>I'll PM you later.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I think the leadership system might benefit from a random events table provided that the human element of it focused on things that could've been going on beneath the PCs notice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Random event tables are sometimes inappropriate, but they are good at inspiring STs. And there's an argument that the issues that leaders must face do include a certain randomness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-14T09:23:31-08:00","id":1348493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347241-what-would-you-like-to-see-in-the-st-guide-crucible-of-legends?p=1348464#post1348464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the leadership system might benefit from a random events table provided that the human element of it focused on things that could've been going on beneath the PCs notice. Also their inner circle are probably full fledged NPCs that the Storyteller wants to behave in a consistent manner.</div> </div> </div> </div>So weird fact, this is why as time has gone on, I think Mande of Heaven was a better &quot;domain&quot; system than Creation-Ruling Mandate. I think the latter assumes a kind of &quot;Seeing like a state&quot; viewpoint I have kind of grown to want to not reify in mechanics myself. (The previous devs, as a note, had this in mind as why they didn't redo it either.) Meanwhile, MoH was in effect a plot-geneartor. Or more notably, a <i>problem</i> generator. And I think had it been streamlined for that better, it'd of done pretty good there.<br /> <br /> I think I've said before, but the supplement for the RPG Godbound called <b>Sixteen Sorrows</b> is actually more what I want out of a &quot;domain&quot; system than the actual domain rules in that game. I think something to generate problems to solve for your projects is more important than trying the taks of having a system represent complex organizations wiout just making it an Objective Problem Solving Machine when Charms come interacting with it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-14T10:05:18-08:00","id":1348503,"title":"","content":"First , I tried reading the thread but didn't get through<br /> <br /> I would like to see some advice for new ST's, some ideas for time saves, something akin to the Mandate system and in general things the help you run the game, play the game and then expand that experience.<br /> <br /> An also some advice on how to jugde custom charms/powers and adventure ideas... like is taking people's powers away from a good idea, if yes how would one apply that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/854-light-hero","name":"light-hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-14T10:32:14-08:00","id":1348514,"title":"","content":"Given Exigents should be the guide to custom charms, I would like there to be active coordination between the Crucible of Legends team and the Exigents team to ensure that together they represent a complete guide to producing custom content for your game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-15T06:53:57-08:00","id":1348660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347241-what-would-you-like-to-see-in-the-st-guide-crucible-of-legends?p=1348493#post1348493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So weird fact, this is why as time has gone on, I think Mande of Heaven was a better &quot;domain&quot; system than Creation-Ruling Mandate. I think the latter assumes a kind of &quot;Seeing like a state&quot; viewpoint I have kind of grown to want to not reify in mechanics myself. (The previous devs, as a note, had this in mind as why they didn't redo it either.) Meanwhile, MoH was in effect a plot-geneartor. Or more notably, a <i>problem</i> generator. And I think had it been streamlined for that better, it'd of done pretty good there.<br /> <br /> I think I've said before, but the supplement for the RPG Godbound called <b>Sixteen Sorrows</b> is actually more what I want out of a &quot;domain&quot; system than the actual domain rules in that game. I think something to generate problems to solve for your projects is more important than trying the taks of having a system represent complex organizations wiout just making it an Objective Problem Solving Machine when Charms come interacting with it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Mandate of Heaven was better to describe the identity of a permanent social group with random problems. Failure: complex mechanics and only downtime.<br /> Creation-Ruling Mandate allowed for detailed features and simple testing (close to the leadership system). Failure: social group without identity and does not generate plot.<br /> <br /> My dream:<br /> &quot;Mandate of Heaven&quot; with Leadership system, Creation-Ruling Mandate attributes and extended in-game testing","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2150-rochedo","name":"Rochedo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2150_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-15T09:51:57-08:00","id":1348681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rochedo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347241-what-would-you-like-to-see-in-the-st-guide-crucible-of-legends?p=1348660#post1348660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Mandate of Heaven was better to describe the identity of a permanent social group with random problems. Failure: complex mechanics and only downtime.<br /> Creation-Ruling Mandate allowed for detailed features and simple testing (close to the leadership system). Failure: social group without identity and does not generate plot.<br /> <br /> My dream:<br /> &quot;Mandate of Heaven&quot; with Leadership system, Creation-Ruling Mandate attributes and extended in-game testing</div> </div> </div> </div>Sudden reboot of my computer kind of ate my reply to this. But I actually kind of disagree on this. CRM has actually more issues than you note.<br /> <br /> The first is it actually more or less has the same issue that Sail does in 3e. It is basically in the end, a bunch of rolls at fixed difficulties or contested rolls that determine success or failure at your endeavours. This means that anyone with the right Excellency breaks the system in half. So while something simpler would be nice, you have to create &quot;buffers&quot; so it doesn't create kind of just this run-away problem rendering it half useless as a result.<br /> <br /> The second is that it kind of reifies issues wiht &quot;seeing like a state&quot;. Actions in CRM really only about obtaining Captial or affecting Assets. Success or failure is determined more or less as to whether you do the thing, which when positively successful, gets you what you want. I think an issue there is that really any failure points are more about whether or not you get to do what you are trying to do. Success or failure is simply whether the leader is competent enough. This includes things like say, improving Competence, which is not about actually rooting out corrupt people or finding good ones, but just improving an abstract stat. It turns societies into systemic logic-engines and makes it difficult to assess people. Note, also, that a lot of the project system we have in 3e, while abstract, does a lot of these with the main conflict point being plot-generating to solve things, not working on asbratced Assets. Basically I think that CRM leans too hard on Civ-style mechanics, as the people in an organization aren't really people, just traits. A bit why 3e doesn't have these systems is in part becuase to my understanding, the devs for the corebook do subscribe to a bit of James C. Scott here.<br /> <br /> Kind of related to that too, note is that success doesn't necssarily mean good. But the way CRM is structured, there's no way to do that. Like, remember that a lot of fammines were done by very successfully implemented land reform built on shoddy ideas. Or that some things like highly currated forests for industrial scale lumber harvesting had great short term but long term catostrophic effects. Or even just odd down-stream stuff like how corruption often comes up due to individual action and sorta spreads if not taken care of, not becuase a trait in the organization is bad. These are in CRM, not replicatable. They arguably do what looks ot be a success, but result in actual problems/failure. CRM only measures whetherw hat you do is doable, not whether it's useful/generates story.<br /> <br /> Thirdly, both CRM and MoH depend on the ST doing too much effing work. A big thing both kind of assume is that you as an ST have an ecosystem of just-as-complex-as-the-PC's stuff going on around for them to interact with, otherwise you hae captial or other sacks of good sitting around for htem to hit like a pi\u00f1ata. Any system needs to have it so that the ST doesn't have to have these effing things prepared or at least not have to have them banging around in the background like NPC Civs in order for it to be less tedious. This is ranodm personal experience having used both before.<br /> <br /> Again, this is all a bit why I think what we need more is 1) Bureacracy just needs like, example show to use it like we have for Larceny and such. It need not be an entire infrastructure system, whcih seems to be what folks have conflated it as being since ever.<br /> <br /> And 2) Probably very very abstracted traits to help us get an idea of what organizaitons have, want, and can do. And what problems might arise. I think here, just giving clearer ideas of the Merits, sizes, and experitse of groups migtht help, but in this regard I think just giving more guideliens on the features of projects from the corebook go just as far as going and trying to make yet another system someone wiht the Excellency will trivialize anyhow, and which somehow tries to capture a successful bar shop to the probably once-in-history Veneician Arsenal (which probably in Exalted is an example of what you can do with the Artifact system without it <i>actually</i> being an Artifact IMHO).<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-15T12:36:57-08:00","id":1348704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347241-what-would-you-like-to-see-in-the-st-guide-crucible-of-legends?p=1347298#post1347298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or even just examples of how it is used honestly. I don't think it need be (Or even shoudl be) CRM. But like...examples of what you acutally <i>do</i> with the Ability wouldn't hurt. SImilar with Occult, Survival, and a few other Abilities to be honest.<br /> <br /> Mind, this has been apparently something mentioned as to will be the case.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would also like this","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-15T12:54:06-08:00","id":1348709,"title":"","content":"I think the project system in the core is fine...but I would appreciate more advice on how to use it effectively. Also ways to tie it into various backgrounds. Maybe some general notes on how long various types of projects might take. Even if it was just \u201cSimple projects are these sorts of things and they usually take this long, Complex projects are this and they take that long, etc\u201d would be nice. And it would help tie in some of the Solar charms too.<br /> <br /> Maybe a discussion on setting difficulties? Including when to go beyond difficulty 5. I mean, I\u2019ve seen crazy numbers of successes on various rolls, but it can be unclear when to allow the Exalted to get away with impossible feats without specific charm backing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-15T21:08:24-08:00","id":1348785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347241-what-would-you-like-to-see-in-the-st-guide-crucible-of-legends?p=1348709#post1348709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the project system in the core is fine...but I would appreciate more advice on how to use it effectively. Also ways to tie it into various backgrounds. Maybe some general notes on how long various types of projects might take. Even if it was just \u201cSimple projects are these sorts of things and they usually take this long, Complex projects are this and they take that long, etc\u201d would be nice. And it would help tie in some of the Solar charms too.<br /> <br /> Maybe a discussion on setting difficulties? Including when to go beyond difficulty 5. I mean, I\u2019ve seen crazy numbers of successes on various rolls, but it can be unclear when to allow the Exalted to get away with impossible feats without specific charm backing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd be all on board for this sorta thing myself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T08:32:52-08:00","id":1351483,"title":"","content":"You know... when somebody said &quot;Hey guys, we're gonna make and Exalted Third Edition&quot;, and we were all hyped as hell, and then somebody said &quot;And we're adding new super secret awesome exalts to the game&quot;, we were even more hyped.<br /> <br /> But then, a crap-ton of time passed and the super secret was kept indefinately for some more time, we only got one caste name, some horrible illustrations in the core, and... suddenly the secret became not so cool anymore. To me, it became a nuisance. It felt like we were not ready to handle this massive great concept. But then the new Devs have been a bit more open to reveal some new bits about it.<br /> <br /> So, I wish the ST guide gave us a huge chunk of info on the new Exalts, I understand that they cannot give full details since not everything has been planned for them, but we need at least enough so that people can homebrew their own stuff. It has been quite boring to know terms like &quot;Umbral Exalted&quot; and be able to do nothing with them in our games. Back in first edition, we were making abyssals and sidereals from day one even if we had no idea that sidereal martial arts existed or what would be the circles of necromancy. We were given interesting pieces, and when we learned that all that we did was &quot;cannonicaly wrong&quot;, guess what, we were even more excited!<br /> <br /> In short: we need disclosure about the new exalts, let us play with them, we will be grateful for their complete rules when they come, but don't put them in a glass case, that is not fun.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T10:30:18-08:00","id":1351509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347241-what-would-you-like-to-see-in-the-st-guide-crucible-of-legends?p=1351483#post1351483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know... when somebody said &quot;Hey guys, we're gonna make and Exalted Third Edition&quot;, and we were all hyped as hell, and then somebody said &quot;And we're adding new super secret awesome exalts to the game&quot;, we were even more hyped.<br /> <br /> But then, a crap-ton of time passed and the super secret was kept indefinately for some more time, we only got one caste name, some horrible illustrations in the core, and... suddenly the secret became not so cool anymore. To me, it became a nuisance. It felt like we were not ready to handle this massive great concept. But then the new Devs have been a bit more open to reveal some new bits about it.<br /> <br /> So, I wish the ST guide gave us a huge chunk of info on the new Exalts, I understand that they cannot give full details since not everything has been planned for them, but we need at least enough so that people can homebrew their own stuff. It has been quite boring to know terms like &quot;Umbral Exalted&quot; and be able to do nothing with them in our games. Back in first edition, we were making abyssals and sidereals from day one even if we had no idea that sidereal martial arts existed or what would be the circles of necromancy. We were given interesting pieces, and when we learned that all that we did was &quot;cannonicaly wrong&quot;, guess what, we were even more excited!<br /> <br /> In short: we need disclosure about the new exalts, let us play with them, we will be grateful for their complete rules when they come, but don't put them in a glass case, that is not fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>So far as we know, Getimians, along with Infernals and Alchemicals, are getting corebook-style write-ups with two page spreads, Caste descriptions, sample NPCs, and some info on how thier powers and thematics operate.<br /> <br /> The other three were kind of not as developed when the previous devs were on things, and what theyw ere going to be wasn't known. They are going to be in an Appendix in Exigents, which shows how the Exigents rules can be used for homebrewing Exalts in general. They're gonna be presented as optionally canon too. Basically while there was a lot of ambition with the new Exalt types, the abiltiy for the gameline as it is with constriants on time and energy means they have to be kind of put there. But they'll have enough to make them playable in that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}